exports[`LFG command-only messages > creates help message 1`] = `
{
  "embeds": [
    {
      "color": 12745742,
      "description": "\`/lfg\` groups subcommands for managing **rooms** for Friend Battles.

Rooms:
- are groups of up to 3 players,
- have a code which should be used in Friend Battles,
- have an **owner** with additional privileges within the group.

Want to play? First check \`/lfg status\` for vacant spots in existing rooms. Ask active players whether you can join them!

Use \`/lfg join\` to join a room, or \`/lfg create\` to create one as the owner.

Still missing players? Use \`/lfg ping\` to ping users who have a role dedicated to LFG.
\`/lfg ping\` enters a cooldown period for the pinged role after use.

When you are done playing, use \`/lfg leave\` so other players can see that you are not playing anymore.

In general, please encourage each other to ensure that \`/lfg status\`'s output is always up-to-date.

A room owner may also use the following commands:
- \`/lfg disband\`: Delete their room.
- \`/lfg change-code\`: Change their room's code.
- \`/lfg kick\`: Kick a player from their room.
- \`/lfg transfer\`: Transfer ownership to another player in their room.

Ownership is automatically transferred when the owner leaves the room.
Rooms are deleted when all players leave.

\`/lfg\` subcommands may be used in any channel without fear of spamming as all responses are visible to the user only.

\`/lfg status\` also displays the server's config for the LFG feature as set by admins:
- **LFG channel**: channel to which will be sent a public copy of all responses returned by \`/lfg\` subcommands following successful execution.
- **LFG roles**: roles which may be pinged by \`/lfg ping\`.
- **LFG roles ping cooldown**: time between pings for each role.

Have fun!!",
    },
  ],
  "kind": "NEUTRAL",
}
`;

